## Quick start

This ZIP contains:
- `config.json` — DAB template configuration (scalar fields)
- `agents_manifest.json` — full manifest of your agents and the shared components (tools, retrievers, lakebase) each one uses
{{#hasCICD}}
- CI/CD workflow file
{{/hasCICD}}

### 1. Initialize the DAB project

```bash
databricks bundle init https://github.com/databricks-solutions/agentops-stacks \
  --config-file config.json
```

This scaffolds `{{{projectName}}}/` with the initial agent `{{{initialAgentName}}}` under `src/agents/{{{initialAgentName}}}/` and shared components under `src/components/`.
{{#hasMultipleAgents}}

### 2. Add the remaining agents

You designed **{{{agentCount}}}** agents on the canvas, but `databricks bundle init` scaffolds only the first one. Add the rest with the agentops-stacks `add-agent` skill (or `add_agent.py`), then wire each one to its components per `agents_manifest.json`:

```bash
cd {{{projectName}}}
# for each additional agent in agents_manifest.json:
#   /add-agent  (or)  python plugin/skills/agentops-stacks/scripts/add_agent.py --name <agent> --from {{{initialAgentName}}}
```

Agents are peers — they don't call each other. Components (tools, retrievers, lakebase) wired to more than one agent are shared under `src/components/` and reused.
{{/hasMultipleAgents}}

